Package: reditR
Type: Package
Title: Differential RNA Editing Analysis for Bulk and Single-Cell Pseudobulk Data
Version: 0.2.3
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Saanvi",
           family = "Jiteendra",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "sj1825@ic.ac.uk")
Description: Statistical tools for detecting differentially edited RNA sites
    from per-site, per-sample read-count tables, whether those samples are
    real bulk RNA-seq replicates or single-cell data aggregated by cluster
    (pseudobulk) -- the underlying binomial count-table format is the same
    either way. Offers three independent significance tests -- a binomial
    generalised linear mixed model (GLMM), Fisher's exact test, and Wilcoxon
    rank-sum -- each run on all sites and independently FDR-corrected, so
    the user can pick whichever test suits their experimental design rather
    than trusting a single combined verdict. Designed for use downstream of
    editing-site detection pipelines such as SPRINT. Includes simulation
    utilities for power analysis and method validation.
